s winning chances from 86% to 55% (−0.55).","40…Rf1+ takes the open f-file and joins the attack on the king.","It prepares …Rc1: the rook clears the way.","White answers 41.Kg2, winning a pawn."]},{"ply":84,"name":"42…d2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"42…d2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Pushes the passed pawn to d2, close to promotion.","Takes c1 away from the rook on c6.","The next best move, 42…Rg1+, would drop Black's winning chances from 87% to 52% (−0.27).","42…d2 pushes the passed pawn to d2.","White answers 43.Kg5, attacking the g6 pawn, which is undefended, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on d2.","Engine line: 43.Kg5 Ke2 44.Re6+ Kf2 45.Rf6+ Kg2 (−5.67)."]},{"ply":100,"name":"50…gxh5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"50…gxh5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the pawn on h5.","Creates a passed pawn on h5: no enemy pawn can stop it any more.","The next best move, 50…Ra5+, would drop Black's winning chances from 99% to 86% (−4.82).","50…gxh5 wins a pawn.","Takes the h5 pawn and wins a pawn once the captures settle.","White answers 51.Kf5, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on h4."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Pawn, Mengarini Attack","eco":"E60","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 3.Qc2: 5 moves in all, 3 by White and 2 by Black.","Theory runs out after 3.Qc2: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}